<p>President Trump said the United States will hold off on threatened strikes on Iranian energy facilities for 10 more days and extend his deadline for Iran to reopen the Strait of Hormuz until April 6 at 8 p.m. Eastern time. Trump said talks with Iran were &quot;going very well&quot; and tied the extension to an Iranian request. Iranian officials, though, publicly denied any negotiations with Washington, underscoring how far apart the two sides remain even with a possible diplomatic off-ramp still on the table. The move briefly lowered the immediate risk of new US strikes on Iran’s power and energy infrastructure, a key point for global oil flows because the Strait of Hormuz is a vital shipping chokepoint for crude exports. But the broader conflict is still active: Iran has kept tightening control over the strait, and traders have pushed oil prices higher while driving a sharp stock-market sell-off as they weigh the risk of escalation against the hope of negotiations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/wc_zL0jJNvlD1XyUphn2KO-75rD791Mzkw4LBITwisE-eJEVcR9sPJTgaaSurlfvjy_YxZXUOV04ha2-8-pbcoJ0YntGh6jjI9GXP2KIaxhUe4I-kaAMCM-F10GpyhyDKzZJVC6kvT-Oin-mptL1wm9c5WNs4oWYcTDPEtdRpQpR-YReyYHXK10DE1cOGCN7R57mDVl3' alt='President Trump, with Secretary of State Marco Rubio, left, and Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth, at the White House on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Market skepticism: The sell-off suggested investors were discounting Washington’s upbeat public messaging and treating the extension as a temporary pause in an unresolved energy shock.</li><li>Symbolic passage: Trump called the movement of 10 tankers through Hormuz an Iranian &quot;gift,&quot; giving traders a limited operational signal about conditions in the waterway even though the wider dispute remains unresolved.</li><li>Mixed signals: Even as Trump said talks were &quot;going very well,&quot; Washington was reportedly considering redirecting weapons originally intended for Ukraine and planning more regional deployments, reinforcing doubts that de-escalation is close.</li></ul><blockquote>Talks are ongoing and, despite erroneous statements to the contrary by the Fake News Media, and others, they are going very well. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: President Trump says Tehran requested the pause, insists negotiations are progressing, and pairs that message with a warning that Iran must reopen Hormuz or face renewed attacks on energy infrastructure. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/trump-extends-deadline-for-iran-to-reopen-oil-route-or-face-power-plant-strikes'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iranian government: Iranian officials have denied holding talks with Washington and rejected US pressure framed as ultimatums, signaling that Tehran does not accept the public US account of the diplomatic track. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/26/nx-s1-5761378/the-u-s-and-iran-cant-even-agree-on-whether-theyre-talking'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Iranian parliament speaker: Iran’s speaker warned that the United States cannot impose ultimatums, reflecting Tehran’s broader view that diplomacy cannot move forward under threat of force. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-cant-issue-ultimatum-irans-speakers-warning-after-trumps-war-pause-11272962#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>US envoy Steve Witkoff: Witkoff floated an Iran peace plan as Washington searched for a negotiated formula alongside military pressure, suggesting that parts of the administration are actively trying to build an offramp. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-israel-tehran-denies-ceasefire-talks-strait-of-hormuz/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Market participants: Financial markets have treated the mixed signals cautiously, with traders focusing less on official optimism and more on the risk that shipping disruption and military escalation could keep energy costs elevated. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/6fc9a9f5-ce8f-471a-a4d2-2166d63e3bd8'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/trump-extends-deadline-for-iran-to-reopen-oil-route-or-face-power-plant-strikes'>Trump extends deadline for Iran to reopen oil route or face power plant strikes</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/diplomacy/article/3348058/trump-claims-iran-begging-make-deal-teases-new-aid-farmers-amid-war-fallout'>Trump claims Iran ‘begging to make a deal’ but teases new aid for farmers amid war fallout</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-stocks-sink-as-trump-pushes-back-hormuz-deadline/live-76555531'>Iran war: Stocks sink as Trump pushes back Hormuz deadline</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/27/iran-war-live-updates-trump-negotiations-bombing-hormuz-energy-oil-prices-middle-east'>Middle East crisis live: Trump pausing strikes on Iran energy sites; Houthis say ‘no reason’ to halt Red Sea shipping</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/26/nx-s1-5761378/the-u-s-and-iran-cant-even-agree-on-whether-theyre-talking'>The U.S. and Iran can&#x27;t even agree on whether they&#x27;re talking</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-israel-tehran-denies-ceasefire-talks-strait-of-hormuz/'>Witkoff floats Iran peace plan as Trump extends pause on energy plant strikes</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-news-cant-issue-ultimatum-irans-speakers-warning-after-trumps-war-pause-11272962#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;Can&#x27;t Issue Ultimatum&quot;: Iran&#x27;s Speaker&#x27;s Warning After Trump&#x27;s War Pause</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/26/2026/trump-extends-deadline-for-iran-to-open-strait-of-hormuz'>Trump extends deadline for Iran to open Hormuz</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/6fc9a9f5